title: 'monitor: nonce_replay backoff should not disable relay permanently without recovery path'
updated_at: "2026-07-14T09:03:37Z"
---
## Problem
Relay peek hits nonce_replay (attempt 1, 2 with backoff) then escalates to TERMINAL timestamp_out_of_window and disables relay watch entirely with \"will not self-heal\". Local watch continues. Operator must re-register and/or restart monitor. Even if B178 fixes the -30.5s skew root cause, terminal disable without a recovery budget is harsh for transient relay glitches.

## Expected
- Transient relay errors stay transient: bounded retries, then slow poll, then optional re-auth
- TERMINAL only for true config/auth breakages (missing key, revoked lease)
- On TERMINAL, emit structured remediation and optionally attempt re-register if configured

## Actual
Two nonce_replays -> TERMINAL disable; false guidance to fix clock/key when issue may be backoff/nonce state.

## Related
B178 filed for the skew symptom; this bug is about monitor policy/resilience.

## Suggested fix
Separate error classes: retryable (nonce, 5xx, timeout) vs fatal (unauthorized unbound, permanent 401). Retryable never permanently disables without N consecutive failures over M minutes.